Faecal Sludge Management — Strande, Ronteltap and Brdjanovic (@wu-fsm: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_2CSTH41F4C2WWARQ7X0ZF5NNGY
Linda Strande, Mariska Ronteltap and Damir Brdjanovic, editors. Faecal Sludge Management: Systems Approach for Implementation and Operation, IWA Publishing, 2014. [Eawag's official book and chapter downloads](https://www.eawag.ch/en/department/sandec/publications/fsm-book/) · [Persistent edition reference](https://doi.org/10.26530/OAPEN_578132).

Read the full systems account, connecting sludge characteristics and treatment with emptying, transport, operation, institutions, finance and implementation. Return to the relevant treatment chapter when comparing liquid/solid separation and receiving routes. Keep the service chain visible: a technically plausible unit does not ensure that material reaches it or that its outputs have a suitable destination.

The indexed institutional download page was checked on 30 October 2026; direct automated retrieval returned HTTP 403. It provides an authorized public reading route, but this Record does not assert a blanket adaptation licence or full-text inspection. Retain the selected edition's rights notice and component credits. Compare historical examples with current local practice and requirements.

